    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full test suite passes (the project has one runnable test class, `AcceptanceTest`, plus support classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment for owner creation. When an owner is created via `POST /api/owners`, they now receive a code formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field (`customer_code` column) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, the code is computed and set before saving via a new `nextCustomerCode(lastName)` helper:\n   - `LAST3` = first three letters of `lastName`, upper-cased (`Locale.ROOT`), tolerating names shorter than 3.\n   - `NNNN` = `String.format(\"%04d\", findAllOwners().size() + 1)` \u2014 a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count. Counting before the save yields consecutive codes (e.g. `SMI-0007` then the next is `+1`).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it (MapStruct auto-maps it by name; no mapper change needed).\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table.\n\n5. **`hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 the seed inserts use column-less `VALUES`, so I appended a trailing `NULL` for the new column to each of the 10 owner rows (the other DBs' seed files use explicit column lists and needed no change).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` \u2014 which asserts the `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and that consecutive owners' sequence numbers differ by exactly 1 \u2014 passes.",
